window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p>Twenty years ago, I loved a woman.</p> <p>Twenty years ago, I also loved a man.</p> <p>And 20 years ago, rather than choose, I abandoned them both.</p> <p>Now, I’m living a lonely life, luckless in love and unwilling to confront the truth of what I left behind.</p> <p>When my brother passes, I become responsible for my four-year-old niece. Uprooting her isn't an option which means heading back to the sticks of New Hampshire, to the small town I fled.</p> <p>Because of Charlotte.</p> <p>Because of Liam.</p> <p>My two best friends, the ones I’d been reluctant to pursue but couldn’t deny.</p> <p>Attempting to avoid facing my past doesn’t work, and I see them both - together. They appear to have moved on while I can’t.</p> <p>I still want her.</p> <p>I still want him.</p> <p>But secrets lay between us, betrayals that threaten to crack the egg shells we walk on.</p> <p>I’ve got more than my own heart to look out for now, and I’ll protect those I love this time around.</p> <p>No matter the cost.</p>"; 
